From 972df6282be156fc15d57e883b520ae350a4987a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alphi <fork@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:20:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: gemjucewindow never waits on the message thread
 under the Pd lock

create() and destroyMess() run inside a Pd message, so their thread (audio
thread, or any thread that delivers a message under sys_lock) holds the Pd
lock. Both called MessageManager::callSync. If the message thread meanwhile
wants the Pd lock (the window's own key/modifier timer, a mouse event over
the Gem window, any plugdata GUI update), neither side moves: hard freeze.
Reproduced with a create/destroy loop; stacks: audio thread in
gemjucewindow::callOnMessageThread <- destroyMess, main thread in
pthread_mutex_lock <- gemjucewindow::Window::timerCallback.

destroy: the window is cut loose from its owner under the Pd lock (atomic
m_owner cleared) and deleted later on the message thread (callAsync). Every
Window callback that reaches the owner takes the Pd lock and checks the
owner first; the resized() callAsync path no longer captures a raw `this`.

create: the Window is built on the message thread by a posted callAsync,
under the Pd lock, and parked; a Pd clock (Pd lock held) picks it up and does
the GL half (makeCurrent, createGemWindow, title, size) on the Pd thread.
create() called on the message thread itself still builds directly.
Messages before the window exists are safe: dimen/offset reach a parked
window or are read by the queued construction; render returns early;
destroy (or freeing the object) drops a queued construction (generation
ticket, shared so a freed object is never touched) and deletes a parked one;
a second create while one is pending says "window already made!".
